# one step at a time is fine until you do not know the way. `jump` asks the
# same question with a distance on it: name the kind you are after and it says
# which routes reach it.
add record username-of
jump ip
# what it prints is an add path, so finding a route and taking it stay two
# acts — `add` is still the only thing that changes anything.
add notes/ip
# the middle of a jumped route is a column you stepped over rather than read,
# and here it is a BitLocker recovery key. shortening is not automatic: a
# column cannot be known to be a waypoint until you have seen what is in it.
shorten ..
